cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Price discovery between KASE and its foreign co-listing venues"
abstract: >-
  Measures how fast the Kazakhstan Stock Exchange absorbs a foreign price move
  that arrived while it was closed, and how that differs across co-listings with
  and without session overlap. Kaspi.kz trades on KASE and NASDAQ, whose regular
  sessions share no clock time; Kazatomprom and Air Astana trade on KASE and the
  LSE International Order Book, which overlap it. Reports the opening gap and
  intraday drift on the prior foreign move with Newey-West HAC standard errors,
  the dependence of that split on which price is called the open, a conditioning
  test on foreign prices visible during the local session, and a three-pair
  overlap contrast. The bar store is not redistributed; data/README.md describes
  how to attach it.
type: software
authors:
